ROADMAP.md:447:| R-0596 | `Secret<T>` with its noninterference and constant-time proofs, from slice 7 ([decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-project-infoflow-2026-11-06)) | at slice 7, scalar `Secret<T>`, `classify` (of a value passed in), `declassify(x, "reason")`, `ct_select` and secret comparisons land; secret control flow, secret indices and secret lengths are refused; scalar secrets are `Copy`; under the randomness decision, the entropy capability arrives at slice 6, its output is `Secret<T>` at slice 7 and fill-bytes arrives at slice 15, with its source a named trusted premise in facts ([decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-07-stack-randomness)); later increments add `ct_eq` on arrays and views and linear, wiped secret arrays at slice 15, wiped heap secrets at slice 19, and grant-backed sources at slices 16, 18 and 27; noninterference and constant time are proved for the type system under the baseline observer model; each `declassify` is traced in the facts; the legacy `constant_time_tag` is rewritten with `ct_eq`; the LCB plan gains constant-time and wipe preservation, and CI checks the binary constant-time premise; Home: spec (the entropy capability and its trusted premise). Gate: the slice's own acceptance gates ([tracking](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-07-tracking)) | R-0592, R-0575 |
