ROADMAP.md:500:| R-0353 | The release-evidence graph and an offline independent bundle verifier | a hostile bundle is rejected; receipt v1 frozen; a receipt distinguishes "was valid when produced" from current acceptance and revocation (the obligations of legacy R-0430), over the per-compilation certificates of R-0552 | R-0201 |
ROADMAP.md:501:| R-0606 | Named assurance properties per module (owner, 2026-11-06) | each property is separate, named and versioned, with its scope, evidence and coverage; there is no ladder of levels | R-0575 |
ROADMAP.md:507:| R-0119 | Exactly three public flagships with their evidence | graduated and maintained | F |
ROADMAP.md:508:| R-0383 | Packages: manifest, resolution, interfaces, provenance, trust policy | the multi-package workspace passes | F |
ROADMAP.md:509:| R-0149 | Incremental builds equivalent to clean builds | the edit, corruption and substitution matrix passes | R-0383 |
ROADMAP.md:510:| R-0398 | LSP and editor service later, over the shared session ([timing decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-07-tools)) | the editor validation passes; Home: tooling. Gate: the editor validation ([tracking](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-07-tracking)) | R-0149 |
ROADMAP.md:516:| R-0568 | Day-one root infrastructure (T0) | on main beside the old tree: the new root's CI jobs; `required-checks.txt` enforced by `train.sh watch` and `land`; a required-check transition mechanism (an explicit, validated old-to-new job mapping; replacement checks must pass at the exact candidate SHA; a control that dropping a requirement without a mapping is refused; no legacy check is ever marked passed); `ISSUES.tsv` (ID, evidence, owner, severity, closure condition) with its validator and controls; the archive records of the stopped services | R-0562, R-0564 |
ROADMAP.md:517:| R-0558 | Move the old tree to `legacy/` in one train and set up the minimal root. Day one, the root holds the README, this file, AGENTS.md, an empty CHANGELOG, LICENSE, the new build files, `ConcreteSpec/Spec.lean`, `docs/PHILOSOPHY.md`, `docs/decisions.md`, the landing, review and hook scripts, `scripts/oracle/`, `required-checks.txt` and its job mapping, `RETENTION.tsv`, the minimal issue record `ISSUES.tsv` with its validator, and the [2026-11 roadmap archive](docs/archive/roadmap-2026-11/README.md) with its task disposition table. Everything else comes back from `legacy/` when a slice needs it. The status page, the work-queue dispatcher, the fuzz farm, perf tracking and the nightly campaign stop, and each is listed in `RETENTION.tsv` as archived; each returns only with a roadmap task. The ci-3 fuzz corpus, perf history and leanprof data were not copied before the handover (decision row P14) and are not archived. | the root holds only that set; a root check refuses any modification or addition under `legacy/`, and any deletion its `RETENTION.tsv` row does not allow (controls for each); no legacy gate runs; the move lands on both remotes | T0, R-0563, R-0565, owner: approval of the move inventory |
ROADMAP.md:518:| R-0565 | Take the website down at the move (decision row P9, 2026-11-05) | the site's build and Pages deployment stop in the move's change; the published site is unpublished as a documented manual step whose moment the owner confirms (an outward action, never automatic); no frozen playground is served; the old site's sources stay archived under `legacy/` with a `RETENTION.tsv` row | R-0564 |
ROADMAP.md:519:| R-0563 | Operational migration acceptance test (T1), before the move | T0 is on main; on a throwaway branch holding the exact proposed day-one root, a fresh clone builds the candidate (after `train.sh build`, so the candidate tree is what builds) with the candidate's own landing tooling, hooks, runs exact-SHA CI and passes a dry-run landing; negative controls (a broken build, a failing hook gate, a failed required CI job, a missing, skipped or cancelled required check, a SHA mismatch) are each refused for the expected reason at the expected SHA; a check that cannot run on a fallback runner is reported incomplete and blocks landing, never passed; the two-remote landing is proved by the move itself | R-0568, owner: approval of the move inventory |
ROADMAP.md:520:| R-0564 | A pinned, reproducible legacy oracle, independent of `legacy/` | `legacy-compiler-final` builds in an isolated checkout of the tag from a pinned toolchain (`scripts/oracle/ORACLE.lock`) into a recorded digest; the build is published as a release artifact whose identity and SHA-256 are in the lock, fetched and verified by digest on any runner, cached on concrete-ci-2 and rebuildable from the tag alone with a hash check; a missing or mismatched artifact makes the oracle check incomplete, which blocks landing; runner criteria (decision row P13, owner 2026-11-05: concrete-ci-2 and GitHub-hosted runners as a regular second pool): the lock records the release tarball's SHA-256 with the toolchain and flake-lock hashes; landing and oracle runs use separate pools with per-pool CPU and memory limits and at most two heavy runs per machine; jobs that need ci-2's caches run there, and the build, the spec, the gates and the oracle diff also run on the GitHub-hosted x86_64-linux pool, which takes them over when ci-2 is down; a check neither pool can run is incomplete and blocks landing, and a heavy campaign the GitHub pool cannot run is recorded as skipped, never passed; self-hosted runners never run pull-request jobs; a weekly from-scratch rebuild matches the digest; the differential harness invokes it by digest when the new compiler changes; an unexplained difference fails, and the oracle's agreement never overrides the Lean semantics | — |
ROADMAP.md:521:| R-0547 | Measurement: per-branch stage timestamps and the median time to land | every landing has its four timestamps, and the median shows here | — |
ROADMAP.md:522:| R-0544 | Review discipline: per slice, delta after the first pass | median ≤ 5 rounds; a slice past 5 is split | — |
ROADMAP.md:523:| R-0545 | Branch discipline: one bug or one rule per branch | a month of landings with no unrecorded bundling | — |
ROADMAP.md:524:| R-0543 | Load control: at most 2 heavy local runs per machine | a third heavy run waits (control) | — |
ROADMAP.md:525:| R-0542 | Generated ledgers with a single hand-edited source | two branches adding records rebase without conflicts | — |
ROADMAP.md:526:| R-0540 | CI tiers: a landing tier for merge, campaigns on schedule | landing tier median ≤ 40 min over 10 runs | — |
ROADMAP.md:527:| R-0539 | Landing trains through `scripts/land/train.sh` | three trains of two or more branches land, median under 2 h | R-0542, R-0540 |
ROADMAP.md:528:| R-0541 | Self-hosted runners never for `pull_request`; heavy runs on the servers | the workflow check and its negative control | R-0543, R-0540 |
ROADMAP.md:529:| R-0513 | Gates that are trustworthy and affordable: inventories over counts, impact-selected pre-push | pre-push median ≤ 10 min, and no gate failure first seen in CI over 20 landings | R-0547 |
ROADMAP.md:530:| R-0546 | Build and compile caches, after profiling the slowest gates | a second run takes at most half the first; changing an identity invalidates the cache (control) | R-0547 |
ROADMAP.md:550:| rocksdb-slice1 | — | RocksDB slice 1 groundwork (R-0285) | `rocksdb-slice1` | `094e51bf3258` | blocked by 0b (incl. bug 102), 2i, 2q | not run | not run | not run | RocksDB slice 1 acceptance, then the four-adapter checkpoint | 2026-11-02: paused until its constructs are supported by the new compiler. landed on main at 094e51bf but not accepted: exits 0b (bug 102), 2i and 2q; G1 (declaring the native library, so it builds with no manual flags) closed by `[native]` ([NATIVE_LIBRARIES.md](legacy/docs/platform/NATIVE_LIBRARIES.md)); G3 closed (bug 103 fixed on main by `0c507fb9`, verified 2026-10-21) |
ROADMAP.md:551:| v1-design-examples | — | V1 design examples (R-0511, row 3) | `v1-design-examples` | `03d2edec1d21` | none (isolated proof development) | not run | not run | not run | V1a's Core interfaces freeze | 2026-11-02: research input for phase A, not an accepted compiler deliverable. landed on main at 03d2edec but not accepted: review of the design questions, then stages (b) and (c) |
